From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:24:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/25] REIMS_VGPU_VBLANK=1 re-raises an idle
 display's present interrupt

A guest display that has gone a whole refresh period without a present raises
the present interrupt (2) again for the frame it presented last, once a period,
phase-locked to that frame's completion, as a display scanning it out at each
vblank would. Nothing else in the page changes (present count, presented
surface, fieldfa4) and there is no GPU work. It starts with the first present,
yields to every present, stops while the guest sleeps (bit 0), is paused or
restoring, or loses its client, and starts again with the next present. The
period is the host modes' highest refresh rate (24-240 Hz), else 60 Hz. Each
tick is a trace event (vblank <k> <enabledInterrupts>); the first tick logs the
guest's enabled interrupt bits. Off unless the variable is 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
